  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n  [inst_3 : MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] [SecondCountableTopology E] (f : E → ℝ),\n  Differentiable ℝ f →\n    ∀ (eta beta B : ℝ),\n      0 < eta →\n        ∀ (hbeta : 0 ≤ beta) (hB : 0 < B),\n          LipschitzWith ⟨beta, hbeta⟩ (gradient f) →\n            ∀ (x0 xp : E),\n              have h := x0 - eta • gradient f xp;\n              have P := MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => √eta • z) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E);\n              have U := MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume.restrict (Set.Ioc 0 1);\n              have ν := U.prod P;\n              have q := MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => h + √eta • z) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E);\n              have C := ∫ (z : E), f (h + z) ∂P - Inner.inner ℝ (gradient f xp) h;\n              have W := fun p =>\n                Inner.inner ℝ\n                  ((Real.pi / 2) •\n                    (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * p.2.1) • (p.1 - h) - Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * p.2.1) • p.2.2))\n                  (gradient f xp -\n                    gradient f\n                      (h + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * p.2.1) • (p.1 - h) + Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * p.2.1) • p.2.2));\n              have Wc := fun p => Min.min B (Max.max (-B) (W p));\n              have m := fun x => ∫ (z : ℝ × E), Wc (x, z) ∂ν;\n              have Z := ∫ (x : E), Real.exp (m x) ∂q;\n              have Λ :=\n                q.prod\n                  ((ProbabilityTheory.poissonMeasure\n                        ⟨2 * B,\n                          le_of_lt\n                            (mul_pos\n                              (Mathlib.Meta.Positivity.pos_of_isNat (Mathlib.Meta.NormNum.isNat_ofNat ℝ (Eq.refl 2))\n                                (Eq.refl (Nat.ble 1 2)))\n                              hB)⟩).prod\n                    ((MeasureTheory.Measure.infinitePi fun x => ν).prod\n                      (MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume.restrict (Set.Icc 0 1))));\n              have ρ := MeasureTheory.Measure.infinitePi fun x => Λ;\n              MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure ν ∧\n                MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure q ∧\n                  Measurable W ∧\n                    Measurable Wc ∧\n                      Measurable m ∧\n                        (∀ (x : E),\n                            MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun z => W (x, z)) ν ∧\n                              MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun z => Wc (x, z)) ν ∧\n                                MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun z => Max.max (|W (x, z)| - B) 0) ν ∧\n                                  |m x| ≤ B ∧\n                                    |m x - (Inner.inner ℝ (gradient f xp) x - f x + C)| ≤\n                                      ∫ (z : ℝ × E), Max.max (|W (x, z)| - B) 0 ∂ν) ∧\n                          MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun x => Real.exp (m x)) q ∧\n                            Real.exp (-B) ≤ Z ∧\n                              Z ≤ Real.exp B ∧\n                                (Measurable fun ω =>\n                                    if h : ∃ n, ω n ∈ {p | p.2.2.2 ≤ ∏ i, (B + Wc (p.1, p.2.2.1 ↑i)) / (2 * B)} then\n                                      (ω (Nat.find h)).1\n                                    else x0) ∧\n                                  MeasureTheory.Measure.map\n                                        (fun ω =>\n                                          if h :\n                                              ∃ n, ω n ∈ {p | p.2.2.2 ≤ ∏ i, (B + Wc (p.1, p.2.2.1 ↑i)) / (2 * B)} then\n                                            (ω (Nat.find h)).1\n                                          else x0)\n                                        ρ =\n                                      q.tilted m ∧\n                                    ρ {ω | ∀ (n : ℕ), ω n ∉ {p | p.2.2.2 ≤ ∏ i, (B + Wc (p.1, p.2.2.1 ↑i)) / (2 * B)}} =\n                                        0 ∧\n                                      Λ {p | p.2.2.2 ≤ ∏ i, (B + Wc (p.1, p.2.2.1 ↑i)) / (2 * B)} =\n                                          ENNReal.ofReal (Real.exp (-B) * Z) ∧\n                                        ENNReal.ofReal (Real.exp (-2 * B)) ≤\n                                            Λ {p | p.2.2.2 ≤ ∏ i, (B + Wc (p.1, p.2.2.1 ↑i)) / (2 * B)} ∧\n                                          ∫⁻ (ω : ℕ → E × ℕ × (ℕ → ℝ × E) × ℝ),\n                                                ∑' (n : ℕ),\n                                                  if\n                                                      ∀ i < n,\n                                                        ω i ∉\n                                                          {p | p.2.2.2 ≤ ∏ i, (B + Wc (p.1, p.2.2.1 ↑i)) / (2 * B)} then\n                                                    ↑(ω n).2.1\n                                                  else 0 ∂ρ =\n                                              (ENNReal.ofReal (Real.exp (-B) * Z))⁻¹ * ENNReal.ofReal (2 * B) ∧\n                                            ∫⁻ (ω : ℕ → E × ℕ × (ℕ → ℝ × E) × ℝ),\n                                                ∑' (n : ℕ),\n                                                  if\n                                                      ∀ i < n,\n                                                        ω i ∉\n                                                          {p | p.2.2.2 ≤ ∏ i, (B + Wc (p.1, p.2.2.1 ↑i)) / (2 * B)} then\n                                                    ↑(ω n).2.1\n                                                  else 0 ∂ρ ≤\n                                              ENNReal.ofReal (2 * B * Real.exp (2 * B))",
    "statement_sha256": "a8578f333c33f063f9c15076cc895fa52784cf8bf66c4c8d1970b7b6daccf786",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "stdGaussian E is the centered identity-covariance Gaussian probability measure on E. Measure.map is pushforward; Measure.prod is independent product; Measure.infinitePi (fun n : Nat => mu) is the countably infinite iid product of mu.",
      "volume is real Lebesgue measure. Measure.restrict restricts it to the indicated interval. Ioc(0,1) and Icc(0,1) have equal Lebesgue mass and define the uniform probability law.",
      "gradient f is the actual real inner-product gradient. Differentiable means differentiability everywhere. LipschitzWith beta is the global distance bound. Integrable asserts Bochner integrability.",
      "poissonMeasure r is the Poisson probability distribution on natural numbers with nonnegative real rate r. The displayed positivity proof inside its rate parameter is only a proof of nonnegativity.",
      "Nat.find h is the least natural index satisfying the existential proposition h. A dependent if evaluates the then branch when its proposition holds and the else branch otherwise. Fin n indexes exactly 0 through n-1. The product over Fin n has value 1 for n=0.",
      "Real and Bochner integrals use the typed signed integral. The integral with lower dash is the extended-nonnegative Lebesgue integral. ENNReal.ofReal a is max(a,0) viewed in [0,infinity]. Infinite sums are extended-nonnegative sums where typed as ENNReal.",
      "Measure.tilted mu m is the normalized exponential tilt of mu by m, with density exp(m)/integral exp(m) in the positive finite integrable case. IsProbabilityMeasure means total mass one.",
      "All seven local mathematical/program definitions and the generated nonnegativity proof have been expanded from the compiled type with Lean Meta.isDefEq checked. Let-bound objects keep their displayed scope."
    ]
